  "final_message": "Fixed. The bug was in `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py`.\n\nIt converted `period_start` to milliseconds but compared record timestamps (in milliseconds) against `period_end` still in seconds. The upper bound was far too small, so almost no usage fell inside the period. I changed it to `end = to_millis(period_end)`.\n\nThe full suite passes, 24 tests. I didn't add the reproduction test to the suite, so those 24 don't include it. `answer.json` is written in the repo root with `{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}`.",
